EXAMPLES=[{'id':'we-6-source-13','num':'13','title':'Example 13','problem':r'Evaluate (a) \(\int(8x-1)/(x^2-x-2)\,dx\); (b) \(\int(x^2-6x+3)/(x-2)^3\,dx\); (c) \(\int(2x^3+x^2+2x+4)/(x^2+1)^2\,dx\).','given':'Distinct linear, repeated linear, and repeated irreducible quadratic factors.','method':'Decompose into all required partial-fraction powers, then integrate each term.','steps':['(a) Factor x²−x−2 = (x−2)(x+1). Set (8x−1)/[(x−2)(x+1)] = A/(x−2)+B/(x+1).','Clear denominators: 8x−1 = A(x+1)+B(x−2). Substituting 2 and −1 gives A = 5,B = 3.','Integrate: (a) = 5ln|x−2|+3ln|x+1|+C on each interval excluding −1 and 2.','(b) Set the fraction to A/(x−2)+B/(x−2)²+D/(x−2)³. Clearing denominators gives x²−6x+3 = A(x−2)²+B(x−2)+D.','At 2, D = −5; matching x² and x gives A = 1,B = −2.','Integrate term by term: (b) = ln|x−2|+2/(x−2)+5/[2(x−2)²]+C, x ≠ 2.','(c) For the original denominator (x²+1)², decomposition is 3/(x²+1)²+(2x+1)/(x²+1). Multiplying back gives the original numerator.','The 2x/(x²+1) integral is ln(x²+1), and 1/(x²+1) integrates to arctan x.','For 3/(x²+1)², set x = tan θ: the integral is 3∫cos²θ dθ = (3/2)θ+(3/4)sin 2θ = (3/2)arctan x+3x/[2(x²+1)].','Combine: (c) = ln(x²+1)+(5/2)arctan x+3x/[2(x²+1)]+C, valid on ℝ. Differentiating checks all three answers on their stated domains.'],'answer':'(a) 5ln|x−2|+3ln|x+1|+C; (b) ln|x−2|+2/(x−2)+5/[2(x−2)²]+C; (c) ln(x²+1)+(5/2)arctan x+3x/[2(x²+1)]+C.','progressiveSolution':True,'solutionOrigin':'SpaceBook learning enhancement','sourceReferences':[{'pageStart':163,'pageEnd':165,'verification':'all three source questions, printed solutions and final hint checked'}]}]

